# Crusader — a Typical enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 3/12 Typical enemies — 14 life, bribe 60 gold
# enemy: Crusader (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0283.dck "Crusader (Wh, 4th)" [Tier 3 — Manalink 3
#   file dated 2016-02-15; its first 13 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 14 lines (60
#   cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/crusader.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 3)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/crusader.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Typical) — "Crusader" (Original)
#   [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Crusader
22 Plains
4 Crusade
4 Castle
2 Disenchant
4 White Knight
4 Eye for an Eye
2 Morale
4 Pikemen
4 Rainbow Knights
2 Battering Ram
2 Dancing Scimitar
4 Benalish Hero
4 Swords to Plowshares
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Swords to Plowshares
#   .vBlack  2 Black Ward, 1 Swords to Plowshares
#   .vBlue   2 Blue Ward, 1 Swords to Plowshares
#   .vGreen  2 Green Ward, 1 Swords to Plowshares
#   .vRed    2 Red Ward, 1 Swords to Plowshares
#   .vWhite  2 White Ward, 1 Swords to Plowshares
SB: 2 Black Ward
SB: 2 Blue Ward
SB: 2 Green Ward
SB: 2 Red Ward
SB: 2 White Ward
